<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48139" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέμῐτ-θεν</span></b> , old termin. of the gen., as in
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμέθεν, Διόθεν</span>, etc.: freq. with
		Ablatival sense, denoting <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>motion from</i> a place, as in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λεσβόθεν, Ἀβυδόθεν, ἄλλοθεν, οἴκοθεν</span>, etc.:
			so with Preps., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ Τροίηθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.38
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ οὐρανόθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.19
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Adv.</u>
				184.12
			</span></i> sq.: most of the forms in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-οθεν</span> were parox., exc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴκοθεν,
				ἄλλοθεν, πάντοθεν</span> (sts. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παντόθεν</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἔκτοθεν,
				ἔνδοθεν</span>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				191.27
			</span></i> sq. (other exceptions in Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.500
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
